WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.500
The page still displays $10.00.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.710
The submitted request now says unit price: 100 cents.

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:15.830
Flawed endpoint: 201 Created. Two mugs stored at $2.00 total.

4
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:19.390
The correct total was $20.00.

5
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:24.300
The trusted field: unitPriceCents from the request body.

6
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:31.060
A price in a request is a claim, not a fact.

7
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:37.370
The expected price is a comparison value only.

8
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:46.040
One BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction: read catalog, insert order and line snapshot.

9
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.380
Altered request: 409 price_changed, current quote $10.00.

10
00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:59.010
Orders created: 0. Bad quantities and unknown products are rejected.

11
00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:04.120
Page loaded at $10.00. Catalog is now $12.00.

12
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:11.150
409 with the updated quote: $24.00 for two. Orders created: 0.

13
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:17.820
Explicit confirmation of 1200 cents: 201, snapshot $12.00.

14
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:26.990
Mid-transaction reprice by a second connection: blocked. Not a price lock.

15
00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.260
The client requests the purchase. The server determines the price.

16
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.250
Not modelled: taxes, discounts, shipping, inventory, payment.
